## Production Deployment

Install the Ansible collections once:

```bash
ansible-galaxy collection install -r requirements.yml
```

{% if ctx.target %}
Set the server in `inventory.yml` and the environment values under `app_env` in
`group_vars/{{ ctx.environments[0].name }}.yml`, then deploy:

```bash
ansible-playbook playbook.yml
```
{% else %}
Each environment is an inventory group with its values in `group_vars/<environment>.yml`.
The playbook reads the host from `DEPLOY_HOST`, `DEPLOY_USER` and `DEPLOY_SSH_PORT`,
and every name under `app_secrets` from the variable of the same name:

```bash
DEPLOY_HOST=203.0.113.10 DEPLOY_USER=deploy \
  ansible-playbook playbook.yml -e deploy_environment={{ ctx.environments[0].name }} -e image_tag=<tag>
```
{% endif %}
{% if ctx.delivery == "registry" %}

Images are pulled from `{{ ctx.registry }}`: export `REGISTRY_USERNAME` and
`REGISTRY_PASSWORD` (a short-lived token is enough). The host logs out after pulling.
{% elif ctx.delivery == "ssh" %}

Images are copied over SSH: save them next to the playbook before deploying:

```bash
docker save {% for repository in ctx.release_repositories %}{{ repository }}:<tag> {% endfor %}| zstd > images.tar.zst
```
{% endif %}

The release runs from `/opt/<project>`. Secrets the backend generates are created on the
first release and reused afterwards. A failed release restores the previous image tag;
images older than the last {{ ctx.retain }} releases are pruned.

## Hardening: encrypt secrets at rest with ansible-vault

By default, secrets are generated during the build and written to the local
`.env` file in plaintext, and `docker-compose.yml` reads them as `${VAR}`. This
is convenient but leaves secrets unencrypted on the control node and unsafe to
commit. When you need secrets encrypted at rest in source control, `ansible-vault`
is the opt-in upgrade path.

1. Move the sensitive entries from `.env` into `group_vars/all/secrets.yml`
   (Ansible auto-loads this file for every host):

   ```yaml
{% for name in ctx.env_vars %}
   {{ name }}: "your_secret_value"
{% endfor %}
   ```

2. Encrypt the file so it is safe to commit:

   ```bash
   ansible-vault encrypt group_vars/all/secrets.yml
   ```

3. Supply the vault password when running the playbook:

   ```bash
   ansible-playbook -i inventory.yml playbook.yml --ask-vault-pass
   # unattended runs can read the password from a file instead:
   ansible-playbook -i inventory.yml playbook.yml --vault-password-file .vault-pass
   ```

Deploy-time generation remains the default; enable vault only when you need
secrets encrypted at rest.

## Stopping Services

```bash
docker compose down
```

To also remove volumes:

```bash
docker compose down -v
```

## Troubleshooting

### Backend won't start

Check logs:
```bash
docker compose logs app
```

Common issues:
{% if ctx.mongo_local %}
- MongoDB not ready: Wait a few seconds and restart
{% endif %}
- Missing environment variables: Check `.env` file
- Port already in use: Change port in docker-compose.yml

{% if ctx.has_frontend %}
### Frontend shows errors

- Make sure you ran `npm run build` in the frontend directory
- Check that `frontend/dist` exists and contains built files
- Check nginx logs: `docker compose logs frontend`
{% endif %}

### Database connection errors

{% if ctx.mongo_local %}
- MongoDB service should be running: `docker compose ps mongodb`
- Connection string should be: `mongodb://mongodb:27017`
{% else %}
- Check your external MongoDB connection string in `.env`
- Ensure network connectivity from container to MongoDB
{% endif %}
